{"name":"Eggshell Cream","hex":"#f5eedb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eggshell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shell around an egg.","A pale off-white colour, like that of the eggshell of many chickens."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale yellowish-whitish colour, like that of the eggshell.","Exhibiting the thinness, translucency or near-transparency, and fragility of an eggshell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eggshell"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eggshell","blocks":[{"text":"An eggshell is the outer covering of a hard-shelled egg and of some forms of eggs with soft outer cots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Egg-rmh.jpg/330px-Egg-rmh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggshell","wikidata":"Q2731253"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream","wikidata":"Q13228"},{"title":"Eggshell (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color eggshell is meant as a representation of the average color of a chicken egg."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggshell_(color)","wikidata":"Q5347944"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2730433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Pararge_aegeria_egg_with_embryo.jpg/500px-Pararge_aegeria_egg_with_embryo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Pararge_aegeria_egg_with_embryo.jpg/1280px-Pararge_aegeria_egg_with_embryo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Pararge_aegeria_egg_with_embryo.jpg/500px-Pararge_aegeria_egg_with_embryo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Butterfly embryo / caterpillar visible through transparent eggshell","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APararge_aegeria_egg_with_embryo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Egg_in_vinegar.jpg/500px-Egg_in_vinegar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia